      "assessment": "Free Reformed Grand Rapids is a Dutch Reformed immigrant heritage congregation in West Michigan's dense Reformed corridor — the FRCNA emerged from mid-20th-century Dutch Reformed immigration into Canada and the upper Midwest. Holds the Three Forms of Unity strictly, practices experiential Dutch Reformed preaching (the nadere reformatie tradition), and observes the regulative principle with Psalm-heavy worship. Male-only ordination, traditional sexual ethics. Pastor C. Pronk (emeritus) was a longstanding FRCNA voice; verify current pastoral status. A meaningful option for those drawn to the experiential Dutch Reformed tradition.",
